--   979  Postgraduate E3 Balanced Solutions for a Better World Scholarship (Trinity College Dublin, university 81)
--        Same batches/band; the destination scheme for the engineering/natural-science/computer-science carve-out in record 345 (Trinity Global Excellence PG, pass 115)
--   980  Hardiman Research Scholarships (University of Galway, university 283)
--        EUR 25,000 p.a. stipend ('fixed') + tuition fee covered, 4 years, full-time Structured PhD; 2026 call closed (1 Dec 2025 - 6 Feb 2026), next cycle NOT dated => deadline NULL/'not_published', status 'upcoming'
-- Side tables: sources 3112 (TCD E3 page, shared by 978+979) and 3113 (Hardiman overview); university_scholarships 703 (978@81), 704 (979@81), 705 (980@283).
-- Expected counters after this batch: active 549 / retired 179 / active rel-4 23 / future deadlines 194 / max 980.
